<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!--
    Navigation icons, replacing the private-use glyphs from WPF's Segoe MDL2 Assets
    (&#xE8A5; Projects / &#xE7B8; Engines / &#xE90F; Toolchains / &#xE713; Settings).
    That font only exists on Windows; on macOS / Linux it degrades to squares.

    Three side benefits of switching to vector paths: shipped with the app, no font dependency, always crisp on HiDPI.
    Coordinates are always 0–24, scaled to the needed size with Path's Stretch="Uniform" — with one
    exception, Hub.Icon.CheckTick, whose comment explains why it is drawn at its final size instead.
  -->

  <!-- A folder -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Projects">M3 6.2A2 2 0 0 1 5 4.2H9.3L11.4 6.8H19A2 2 0 0 1 21 8.8V17.8A2 2 0 0 1 19 19.8H5A2 2 0 0 1 3 17.8Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- An isometric cube = Engines. The page manages installed engine versions, and the previous glyph
       (a download arrow dropping into a tray) read as "a download list" — it also duplicated the brand
       tile's icon. A cube reads as a self-contained engine unit and matches the game-engine context.
       Built as the silhouette hexagon minus the three inset faces (F0, even-odd), so the rim and the
       face edges come out as even ~0.9-unit lines. Generated by tmp/gen_nav_icons.py. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Installs">M12 3L20 7.5L20 16.5L12 21L4 16.5L4 7.5ZM12 4.03L18.62 7.76L12 11.48L5.38 7.76ZM19.1 8.52L19.1 15.97L12.45 19.71L12.45 12.26ZM4.9 8.52L11.55 12.26L11.55 19.71L4.9 15.97Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- ==================== Brand mark ====================
       The application icon's mark (Assets/hub-icon.svg), on the 0-24 grid so the sidebar carries the real brand
       rather than a decorative square. A DrawingImage rather than a StreamGeometry, unlike every navigation icon
       above it, because the brand is the one mark in this app that is a *gradient* and not a single flat ink.

       Two things here are deliberate and were both wrong in the first attempt:
       1. The pentagon's corners are taken from hub-icon.svg but **re-ordered by angle**. The SVG lists them in
          pentagram order (top, left, right, bottom-left, bottom-right), so joining them in file order draws a
          self-crossing star with concave notches, not the convex pentagon the icon shows. Proved by
          tmp/check_pentagon.py: the turn at each vertex flips sign, and the enclosed area is 29566 where a
          regular pentagon on the same side is 106850.
       2. Sizes are chosen for the 18 DIP the sidebar actually draws, not scaled down from the 512px tile: a
          literal downscale leaves a 3.5%-of-tile hairline ring, nodes that swallow it, and a hub core whose
          ring + disc + sparkle collapse into one blob.
       Contact sheet: x 2.000..22.000, y 2.413..21.587, centre (12, 12). Generated by tmp/gen_brand_logo.py —
       regenerate that script rather than nudging these numbers. -->
  <DrawingImage x:Key="Hub.Image.Brand">
    <DrawingGroup>
      <GeometryDrawing Geometry="M3.55 10.103L12 3.963L20.45 10.103L17.227 20.037L6.773 20.037Z">
        <GeometryDrawing.Pen>
          <Pen Brush="{DynamicResource Hub.BrandGradient}" Thickness="1.4"
               LineCap="Round" LineJoin="Round" />
        </GeometryDrawing.Pen>
      </GeometryDrawing>
      <!-- The hub disc, with the sparkle cut out of it by F0 (even-odd) so the sidebar's own background shows
           through the cut. Its waist is a third of its reach rather than the source icon's hairline, which at
           the ~2px this is drawn at would leave one diagonal sliver instead of four arms. -->
      <GeometryDrawing Brush="{DynamicResource Hub.BrandCore}"
        Geometry="F0 M9.4 12.849A2.6 2.6 0 1 0 14.6 12.849A2.6 2.6 0 1 0 9.4 12.849ZM12 10.899Q12.7 12.149 13.95 12.849Q12.7 13.549 12 14.799Q11.3 13.549 10.05 12.849Q11.3 12.149 12 10.899Z" />
      <GeometryDrawing Brush="{DynamicResource Hub.BrandGradient}"
        Geometry="M2 10.103A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 5.1 10.103A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 2 10.103ZM10.45 3.963A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 13.55 3.963A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 10.45 3.963ZM18.9 10.103A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 22 10.103A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 18.9 10.103ZM15.677 20.037A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 18.777 20.037A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 15.677 20.037ZM5.223 20.037A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 8.323 20.037A1.55 1.55 0 1 0 5.223 20.037Z" />
    </DrawingGroup>
  </DrawingImage>

  <!-- The window-control glyphs are NOT here: the title bar's three caption glyphs are authored 1:1 in the
       12x12 box they are drawn in, so they live in MainWindow.axaml's resources as Hub.Icon.CaptionMaximize /
       Hub.Icon.CaptionRestore. Putting them here on the 0-24 grid and drawing them with Stretch="Uniform" is
       what made the minimize bar render as a dot and then as two lines. -->

  <!-- A hex nut (F0 = even-odd fill rule, which makes the inner circle a cutout) -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Toolchains">F0 M12 2.6L20 7.3V16.7L12 21.4L4 16.7V7.3ZM12 9A3 3 0 1 0 12 15A3 3 0 1 0 12 9Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- An eight-toothed gear with a bore = Settings. This is the shape Font Awesome, Bootstrap Icons
       and VS Code all ship, so it reads as "settings" before it is read closely. The previous icon was
       three sliders, which Material Design popularised but which reads as "filter" when it sits next to
       the folder, tray and hex nut above. Two concentric rings of arcs carry the teeth: radius 7.6 at
       the root, 9.7 at the tip. The trailing circle is the bore, cut out by the even-odd rule (F0), the
       same trick the Toolchains hex nut uses. Generated by tmp/gen_gear_icon.py. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Settings">F0 M10.48 4.55L10.82 2.37A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 13.18 2.37L13.52 4.55A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 16.19 5.66L17.97 4.36A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 19.64 6.03L18.34 7.81A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 19.45 10.48L21.63 10.82A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 21.63 13.18L19.45 13.52A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 18.34 16.19L19.64 17.97A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 17.97 19.64L16.19 18.34A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 13.52 19.45L13.18 21.63A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 10.82 21.63L10.48 19.45A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 7.81 18.34L6.03 19.64A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 4.36 17.97L5.66 16.19A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 4.55 13.52L2.37 13.18A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 2.37 10.82L4.55 10.48A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 5.66 7.81L4.36 6.03A9.7 9.7 0 0 1 6.03 4.36L7.81 5.66A7.6 7.6 0 0 1 10.48 4.55ZM8.4 12A3.6 3.6 0 1 0 15.6 12A3.6 3.6 0 1 0 8.4 12Z</StreamGeometry>
  <!-- A simpler gear outline for small action buttons; the filled sidebar glyph remains separate. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.SettingsOutline">M10 3H14L14.5 5.1L16.2 5.8L18.1 4.7L20.9 7.5L19.8 9.4L20.5 11.1L22.5 11.5V15L20.3 15.5L19.6 17.2L20.7 19L18 21L16 19.9L14.4 20.6L14 22.5H10L9.6 20.6L8 19.9L6 21L3.3 19L4.4 17.2L3.7 15.5L1.5 15V11.5L3.5 11.1L4.2 9.4L3.1 7.5L5.9 4.7L7.8 5.8L9.5 5.1Z M9 13A3 3 0 1 0 15 13A3 3 0 1 0 9 13Z</StreamGeometry>

  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Chevron">M6.4 9.5H17.6L12 16Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A two-stroke caret for the composer's chips. The filled triangle above is right for a combo box at 11
       DIP, but stroked at 9–10 its three edges are closer together than the pen is wide, so it reads as a
       blob. Its bounding box is 11×5.4 centred on 12,12, which is what Stretch="Uniform" needs to keep the
       caret on the text's middle line. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Caret">M6.5 9.3L12 14.7L17.5 9.3</StreamGeometry>

  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Tick">M9.6 16.6L4.4 11.4L2.6 13.2L9.6 20.2L21.4 8.4L19.6 6.6Z</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.MenuTick">M4 12L9 17L20 6</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- The checkbox's tick, and deliberately **not** Hub.Icon.Tick: a Shape with Stretch scales its
       geometry to fit and then pins the result to the box's top-left, so the slack of anything that is
       not box-shaped lands entirely at the right and bottom. The 24-grid tick, stretched into the
       checkbox's 12 DIP slot, filled that slot's width exactly and left all 3.3 DIP of slack at the
       bottom: measured on a drive-mode capture of the settings page, it sat 1.5 DIP high (3 px above,
       6 below) with a stroke thinned to 1 DIP — the off-centre tick this replaced.
       Drawn at the size the template needs instead — ink 12 DIP wide, 8.73 tall, a 1.9 DIP stroke, the
       proportions Material's check uses relative to its box — and centred by layout with
       Stretch="None", which no stretch anchor can move: the same capture then measured 3/3 and 4/4.
       Generated by tmp/tick_final.py. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.CheckTick">M0 5.39L3.33 8.73L12 1.46L10.78 0L3.45 6.15L1.34 4.05Z</StreamGeometry>

  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.ChevronRight">M9 5L16.5 12L9 19L6.5 16.5L11.5 12L6.5 7.5Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A thumbtack pin: head, narrow stem and pointed tip, recognizable at small badge sizes. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Pin">M7 3.5H17L16 10L19 13V14H13V21L12 22L11 21V14H5V13L8 10Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Two offset document outlines = Copy -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Copy">M8 7V5.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 9.5 4H15A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 16.5 5.5V12A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 15 13.5H14 M6 8H11.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 13 9.5V16A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 11.5 17.5H6A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4.5 16V9.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 6 8Z</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Edit">M3.5 16.5L3 21L7.5 20.5L19.2 8.8L15.2 4.8ZM13.8 6.2L17.8 10.2</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.OpenFile">M14 3H21V10 M21 3L11 13 M18 13V19A2 2 0 0 1 16 21H5A2 2 0 0 1 3 19V8A2 2 0 0 1 5 6H11</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Reply">M10 8V4L3 11L10 18V14C15 14 18 16 21 20C20 13 17 8 10 8Z</StreamGeometry>
  <!-- A bin: lid line, handle, tapered body, two ribs. Stroked like Edit, and the same 24x24 box so the two sit
       side by side in the steer-confirm bar without one reading heavier. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Trash">M5 7H19 M9.5 7V5.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 11 4H13A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 14.5 5.5V7 M7 7L7.7 19.1A1.9 1.9 0 0 0 9.6 20.9H14.4A1.9 1.9 0 0 0 16.3 19.1L17 7 M10.2 10.5V17.3 M13.8 10.5V17.3</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.CopySuccess">M4.5 12.5L9.2 17L19.5 6.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A 300° arc with a gap at the top and an arrowhead on its end = regenerate. Stroked. The arc is r=7 on
       centre (12,12) and the arrowhead reaches the same 5.3..19 extent on both axes, so the bounding box is
       square: Stretch="Uniform" leaves any leftover axis as slack, which would push a lopsided glyph off
       centre in its slot. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Refresh">M15.5 5.9A7 7 0 1 1 8.5 5.9M5.3 5.3L8.5 5.9L7.4 8.9</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Browser history arrows: mirrored, square-bounded outlines for the shared small action slot. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Back">M18 12H6 M12 6L6 12L12 18</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Forward">M6 12H18 M12 6L18 12L12 18</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Two chevrons pointing away from each other = unfold: show the whole file instead of the hunks. Stroked,
       and mirrored by Hub.Icon.Fold pointing inward. The pair is the same 8 DIP wide and 15 tall, so the button
       does not move the moment its meaning flips. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Unfold">M8 8.5L12 4.5L16 8.5 M8 15.5L12 19.5L16 15.5</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Fold">M8 4.5L12 8.5L16 4.5 M8 19.5L12 15.5L16 19.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A 300° ring with a 60° gap at the top, no arrowhead = in progress. Unlike Hub.Icon.Refresh,
       it does not suggest the regenerate action. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.InProgress">M15.5 5.9A7 7 0 1 1 8.5 5.9</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A terminal prompt for a command in flight. The > and underscore fit a square box so they stay centred
       in the same 10 DIP status slot used by finished commands and the hover chevron. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.CommandPrompt">M5 5L12 12L5 19M13 19H19</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A git branch = branch a new task from here: the trunk on the left, the current message as its bottom
       node, and a curve leaving for a new node at the top right. Stroked, r=2.2 nodes like the chat-mode
       bullseye. Bounding box is square (15.4 on both axes, centred on 12,12) for the reason above, and the
       curve lands exactly on the trunk node's right edge so the three strokes read as one connected mark. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Branch">M6.5 4.5V15.3M6.5 15.3A2.2 2.2 0 1 0 6.5 19.7A2.2 2.2 0 1 0 6.5 15.3M17.5 4.3A2.2 2.2 0 1 0 17.5 8.7A2.2 2.2 0 1 0 17.5 4.3M17.5 8.7A8.8 8.8 0 0 1 8.7 17.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A speech bubble with a spark = AI assistant. The bubble reads as "chat"; the inner spark keeps it from
       being mistaken for the Projects/Engines icon set at 17px. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Assistant">F1 M4 5.4A1.6 1.6 0 0 1 5.6 3.8H18.4A1.6 1.6 0 0 1 20 5.4V14.6A1.6 1.6 0 0 1 18.4 16.2H11.2L6.6 20.2V16.2H5.6A1.6 1.6 0 0 1 4 14.6ZM12 6.2L13.1 8.7L15.6 9.8L13.1 10.9L12 13.4L10.9 10.9L8.4 9.8L10.9 8.7Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- An upward arrow = send. Drawn as an open path so it is stroked, not filled: a filled arrowhead at
       15px reads as a solid blob, while the caret-plus-stem shape stays legible on the small round button.
       The bounding box is deliberately SQUARE (12x12, centred on the 24 grid): the glyph sits in a square
       slot with Stretch=Uniform, and any leftover axis keeps that slack — which Avalonia leaves on the
       right, so a taller-than-wide arrow renders visibly off-centre. Hub.Icon.Stop keeps its box square for
       the same reason; only its corners are cut. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Send">M12 18V6M6 12L12 6L18 12</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A downward arrow = scroll to the latest message, the vertical mirror of the send glyph. Stroked, and
       square-bounded (12x12 centred) for the same reason Send is. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.ArrowDown">M12 6V18M6 12L12 18L18 12</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A solid rounded square = stop, the same button's other state. It contrasts with the arrow by fill rather
       than by colour, so the two states are distinguishable even in a monochrome screenshot. The corners are
       rounded at r=1.8 on this grid — 19% of the square's side, which measures as ~3 DIP in the 15.5 px the slot
       actually draws, and stays a square rather than drifting toward a circle. Reasons for rounding at all: a
       square corner would be the only hard edge in an otherwise radius-4..15 shell, and a radius small enough to
       blend into the antialiasing reads as a slip rather than as a decision (a 2 DIP corner did). The corners
       only cut the shape — the box stays 9.4 wide and square, centred on 12,12, because Stretch="Uniform" parks
       any leftover axis as slack on one side (see Hub.Icon.Send above). -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Stop">M9.1 7.3H14.9A1.8 1.8 0 0 1 16.7 9.1V14.9A1.8 1.8 0 0 1 14.9 16.7H9.1A1.8 1.8 0 0 1 7.3 14.9V9.1A1.8 1.8 0 0 1 9.1 7.3Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Goal actions: filled pause bars and play triangle, centered in the authored 24-unit viewport. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Pause">M6 5H10V19H6Z M14 5H18V19H14Z</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Play">M6 5L18 12L6 19Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A panel with a divider = sidebar toggle, matching the shape GitHub Copilot Desktop uses. Stroked. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Panel">M4.5 5H19.5V19H4.5 Z M10 5V19</StreamGeometry>
  <!-- A desktop application window: outer frame, title bar, and clear content area. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Application">F0 M3 4H21V20H3Z M5 6V18H19V6Z M5 8H19V9.3H5Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- An information circle for About, square-bounded like the other menu glyphs. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Info">M4 12A8 8 0 0 1 20 12A8 8 0 0 1 4 12ZM12 10.5V16M12 7.5V7.6</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- An open door and outward arrow for Exit, square-bounded like the other menu glyphs. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Exit">M10 4H4V20H10 M10 12H20 M15 7L20 12L15 17</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- The same plate with the divider on the right, so the two top-bar toggles read as a mirrored pair: the left
       one opens the conversation list, this one the review column. Bounded 15×15 centred on the 24 grid —
       deliberately not a copy of Hub.Icon.Panel's 15×14 box, because Stretch="Uniform" parks the leftover axis as
       slack on one side, which puts a lopsided glyph off centre in its square slot. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.PanelRight">M4.5 4.5H19.5V19.5H4.5 Z M14 4.5V19.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- The inspector column's expand/restore pair. Two arrows on the same diagonal, a gap between their tips so
       the two glyphs stay distinguishable at 14px where a merged centre reads as one blob: expand puts the
       arrowhead on the outer corner (it points out, at the window edge), restore puts it on the inner end (it
       points back at the centre). Stroked, and square-bounded (4.5–19.5 on both axes) for the same reason Send
       is — Stretch="Uniform" leaves any leftover axis as slack, which pushes a lopsided glyph off centre. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Expand">M13.5 4.5H19.5V10.5 M19.5 4.5L12.5 11.5 M10.5 19.5H4.5V13.5 M4.5 19.5L11.5 12.5</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Restore">M12.5 5.5V11.5H18.5 M12.5 11.5L19.5 4.5 M11.5 18.5V12.5H5.5 M11.5 12.5L4.5 19.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A magnifier = search. A larger lens and shorter handle share the same centred 15-unit square.
       Cubic curves include the open handle in the bounds; the arc form reports only the lens here. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Search">M4.5 11C4.5 7.4101 7.4101 4.5 11 4.5C14.5899 4.5 17.5 7.4101 17.5 11C17.5 14.5899 14.5899 17.5 11 17.5C7.4101 17.5 4.5 14.5899 4.5 11Z M15.5962 15.5962L19.5 19.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A plus = new. Stroked. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Plus">M12 5.5V18.5 M5.5 12H18.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A four-point sparkle = neutral notice (e.g. model changed). Filled. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Notice">M12 5.5 L13.4 10.6 L18.5 12 L13.4 13.4 L12 18.5 L10.6 13.4 L5.5 12 L10.6 10.6 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Chat modes: a question bubble, a checked plan, and a bullseye goal. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.ChatModeAsk">M5 5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 7.5 3H16.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 19 5.5V13.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 16.5 16H10L6 20V16H7.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 13.5ZM9.6 8.1A2.1 2.1 0 1 1 12 10.2C11.1 10.7 10.8 11.2 10.8 12.1M10.8 14.1V14.2</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.ChatModePlan">M7 4.5H17A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 18.5 6V18A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 17 19.5H7A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 5.5 18V6A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 7 4.5ZM8 9L9 10L11 8M12.5 9H16M8 14L9 15L11 13M12.5 14H16M9 4.5V3.5H15V4.5</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.ChatModeGoal">M12 4A8 8 0 1 0 12 20A8 8 0 1 0 12 4ZM12 7A5 5 0 1 0 12 17A5 5 0 1 0 12 7ZM12 10A2 2 0 1 0 12 14A2 2 0 1 0 12 10Z</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Close">M6.5 6.5L17.5 17.5M17.5 6.5L6.5 17.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Tool permission tiers: a shield (it asks), a play mark (it runs on its own), a warning triangle (it
       never asks). Drawn on the same 24 grid as the chat-mode icons so they sit on one baseline in the menu. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.PermissionAsk">M12 3.6L18.6 6.1V11.4C18.6 15.6 15.8 19 12 20.4C8.2 19 5.4 15.6 5.4 11.4V6.1ZM9.4 11.9L11.3 13.8L14.8 10.3</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.PermissionAuto">M12 3.8A8.2 8.2 0 1 0 12 20.2A8.2 8.2 0 1 0 12 3.8ZM10.4 8.9L15.4 12L10.4 15.1Z</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.PermissionFull">M12 4.2L20.6 19.2H3.4ZM12 9.8V14.2M12 16.6V16.8</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- The session's sandbox: the directory the assistant may read, write and run commands in. Stroked, on the
       same 24 grid as the permission tiers so the composer chips share a baseline. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Folder">M3.6 7.6A2 2 0 0 1 5.6 5.6H9.4L11.4 8H18.4A2 2 0 0 1 20.4 10V16.4A2 2 0 0 1 18.4 18.4H5.6A2 2 0 0 1 3.6 16.4Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- ───────── The bottom menu's appearance glyphs ─────────
       Contrast for the 外观 row, globe for the 语言 row, sun for the 主题 row. Nothing here is drawn per theme
       value any more: the answers under 主题 are names and a tick, so the crescent and the screen that used to
       sit beside 浅色 and 跟随系统 went with the per-value rows that carried them.
       Every glyph here is built so its bounding box is a 16x16 square centred on the 24 grid, because
       Stretch="Uniform" parks any leftover axis as slack on one side (the failure Hub.Icon.Send's comment
       documents, and what FitsItsSquareSlot measures). The trick is that an arc whose endpoints are
       diametrically opposite has its centre forced — chord = 2r leaves exactly one solution — so the box is
       provable from the path rather than judged from a screenshot. -->

  <!-- Contrast, for 外观: the outer circle plus the diameter that splits it, which is what makes the two halves
       two sides of one question. The circle's two halves each span a diameter, so its centre is forced; the
       line joins the circle's own top and bottom points and never leaves the box. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Contrast">M4 12A8 8 0 0 1 20 12A8 8 0 0 1 4 12ZM12 4V20</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A sun, the 主题 row's glyph: a disc with eight rays that stop short of it. The disc and the four axis rays
       fix the box; the diagonal rays stay inside it. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Sun">M8.8 12A3.2 3.2 0 0 1 15.2 12A3.2 3.2 0 0 1 8.8 12ZM12 4V6.8M12 17.2V20M4 12H6.8M17.2 12H20M6.3 6.3L8.3 8.3M15.7 15.7L17.7 17.7M17.7 6.3L15.7 8.3M6.3 17.7L8.3 15.7</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A globe, the 语言 row's glyph: outline circle, a closed meridian, one equator. The circle's two halves and
       the meridian each span a diameter, so both centres are forced; the equator joins the circle's own left
       and right points. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Hub.Icon.Globe">M4 12A8 8 0 0 1 20 12A8 8 0 0 1 4 12ZM12 4A3.8 8 0 0 0 12 20A3.8 8 0 0 0 12 4ZM4 12H20</StreamGeometry>

